"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/deployments","created_at":"2015-04-13T18:04:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T14:39:15Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-29T14:39:07Z","git_url":"git://github.com/apache/airflow.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:apache/airflow.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow","homepage":"https://airflow.apache.org/","size":790917,"stargazers_count":47308,"watchers_count":47308,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":18214,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1927,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["airflow","apache","apache-airflow","automation","dag","data-engineering","data-integration","data-orchestrator","data-pipelines","data-science","elt","etl","machine-learning","mlops","orchestration","python","scheduler","workflow","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/72398","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72398","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72398.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72398.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Extra headers from the HTTP Connection were forwarded by aiohttp on cross-origin redirects (#70164).\n- `HttpAsyncHook` now attaches a per-hop aiohttp client middleware that pops Extra names when a hop leaves the first-request origin.\n- Redirect method rewrite, body/`params`, caller `Authorization`/`Cookie`, http(s) `Location`, `max_redirects`, and `history` stay with aiohttp.\n- The previous redirect walker is removed. It was a partial client: any leftover Extra key forced `allow_redirects=False` and replayed payloads, skipped POST→GET, and forwarded caller credentials.\n- Sync `HttpHook` is unchanged.\n\nThis PR is **async-only**. Other in-flight work covers the same leak from other angles:\n\n- related: #72165\n- related: #70000\n\ncloses: #70164\n\n## Why it happened\n\nHTTP Connection Extra is documented as a place to put credential headers (`X-API-Key`, `Private-Token`, and similar) alongside login/password. `HttpAsyncHook.config` copies every non-reserved Extra key into request headers.\n\naiohttp follows redirects by default. It strips `Authorization` / `Cookie` / `Proxy-Authorization` when the origin changes, but it does **not** strip Connection Extra headers. Those keys stay on the next hop, often a CDN or object store.\n\nA walker that takes over hops whenever Extra has any leftover key (including `Accept`) is the wrong fix. It turns off aiohttp's hop loop and becomes a second, incomplete HTTP client.\n\n## What changed\n\nScope is `HttpAsyncHook` only. Sync `HttpHook` is untouched.\n\n### `providers/http/src/airflow/providers/http/hooks/http.py`\n\n- Keep `_redirect_leaves_origin` and `SessionConfig.connection_headers` (Extra names recorded in `config()` after reserved options are popped).\n- Add `_build_connection_header_middleware`: remember the first `req.url` as the origin; on later hops, if `_redirect_leaves_origin(first, str(req.url))`, pop Extra names from `req.headers` (CIMultiDict is case-insensitive).\n- Do **not** pop caller `Authorization` / `Cookie` / `Proxy-Authorization`. Do **not** clear `auth=`. aiohttp already does that on origin change.\n- When Extra names exist, compose `middlewares=(our_mw, *session._middlewares, *caller_middlewares)` and pass `middlewares=` on the request. Per-request `middlewares=` replaces session middleware, so composition is mandatory.\n- Pass through `allow_redirects` and `max_redirects`. Do not default HEAD to True. Do not force `allow_redirects=False`.\n- Delete the walker (`allow_redirects=False` loop, `urljoin`, `TooManyRedirects`, `_get_redirect_location`, `_DEFAULT_ASYNC_MAX_REDIRECTS`, `_REDIRECT_STATUSES`).\n\n### Origin rule\n\nSame as `requests.Session.should_strip_auth`: a hostname change leaves the origin; `http` on port 80/default to `https` on port 443/default does not; any other scheme or port change does.\n\nOn default-port `http` → `https`, Extra headers stay (requests-shaped). Connection BasicAuth and caller `Authorization` follow aiohttp's origin rules (stricter than the walker).\n\n### Docs\n\n- `providers/http/docs/connections/http.rst` and `providers/http/docs/changelog.rst` now say **origin** (hostname, port, or scheme other than default-port `http` → `https`), not only host.\n\n## How it does it\n\naiohttp ≥3.12 runs client middleware inside the redirect loop, after each `ClientRequest` is built and before `send()`. Popping Extra names from live `req.headers` removes them from the hop that is about to go on the wire. `HttpTrigger` can still pass a bare `ClientSession` into `hook.run(session=session)` — per-request `middlewares=` still applies.\n\n1. Record Extra header names from `SessionConfig.connection_headers`.\n2. If Extra names exist, attach composed middleware and let aiohttp follow redirects.\n3. If Extra is empty, do not attach middleware; native redirects are unchanged.\n4. Middleware first hop: remember origin URL; Extra stays.\n5. Later hops: if the URL leaves that origin, pop Extra names only.\n\n## Test plan\n\nPassed (80 tests):\n\n```bash\nuv run --project providers/http pytest providers/http/tests/unit/http/hooks/test_http.py -xvs\n```\n\n- Middleware unit tests (fake ClientRequest): Extra gone on cross-host / port / hostname change; Extra kept on same-host, relative, and default-port `http` → `https`; caller `Authorization` / `Cookie` / `Proxy-Authorization` left in place; Extra name `Accept` strips Accept only.\n- Extra names recorded; reserved keys such as `max_redirects` are options, not headers.\n- When Extra exists, `middlewares` is passed and `allow_redirects` is not forced `False`.\n- Session and caller middlewares are composed, not replaced.\n- When Extra is empty, no middleware; native redirects (`allow_redirects` omitted).\n- `allow_redirects=False` is still a single call.\n- HEAD + Extra does not pass `allow_redirects=True`.\n- `_redirect_leaves_origin` matches the `should_strip_auth` origin rule.\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes — Cursor Grok 4.6\n\nGenerated-by: Cursor Grok 4.6 following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/72398/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/72398/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]]
